<title>BELGIUM: Luxembourg's SES (Astra) 1996 earnings rocket.</title>
<headline>Luxembourg's SES (Astra) 1996 earnings rocket.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luxembourg-based satellite operator Societe Europeenne des Satellites (SES) said on Tuesday 1996 net profit soared to 4.80 billion Luxembourg francs from 2.88 billion in 1995 and 3.99 billion in 1994.</p>
<p>SES said the earnings growth was partly due to income from the Astra 1E and 1F satellites which started service in 1996. Turnover rose 37 percent to 14.06 billion francs last year.</p>
<p>SES invested 13.30 billion francs to build new satellites and ground control systems in 1996. Four satellites are currently under construction for launch in 1997 and 1998.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
